From d5b29b0385fe9f8f15d8e0ef7d0750718949e0e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:34:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dapf: add the T6050 PMP DART (dart-pmp0)

Add /arm-io/dart-pmp0 to dapf_entries[] so dapf_init programs the T6050 PMP's
DAPF filter. Without it the PMP ASC MMIO window stays fabric-gated and AP access
SYNC-faults (the probe wedge seen in bring-up). dart-pmp0 is dart,t8110 with a
dapf-instance-0 property, which dapf_init -> dapf_init_t8110 already handles; the
DAPF aperture is reg[1] (0x2841b0000), live-verified: after
dapf_init("/arm-io/dart-pmp0", 1) the PMP ASC CPU_CONTROL reads cleanly with 0
exceptions, where a raw read without the filter faulted.

On the proxy path dapf_init_all runs with fdt NULL and opens it regardless of the
alias; on the disk-boot/FDT path the kernel DT aliases pmp0 to the PMP's DART with
status = okay to match this entry. Build only; installing the resident is a
separate step.

[ported from edimoldovan/m1n1 t6050-aurora fc277aa1be by rolotrealanis98,
AI-assisted. Our base (upstream 7cde7d1a) has the two-field dapf_entries[]
with no alias and no FDT gating, so the entry is added without the "pmp0"
alias and dapf_init_all() from kboot_boot() programs it on every stage-2
boot, whatever the kernel DT says. The table is reflowed one entry per line
so the file stays clang-format clean.

J716s (Mac17,8) runtime ADT, read offline: /arm-io/dart-pmp0 is dart,t8110,
reg[1] = 0x2841b0000 size 0x4000 (256 slices), dapf-instance-0 holds 31
entries, the node has an empty clock-gates property (so dapf_init neither
powers it up nor down afterwards) and no allow-dram-apf-slices-0 property
(the one /arm-io/dart-aop carries, which our T6050 AOP skip works around).
/arm-io/dart-pmp does not exist on T6050, so before this change no PMP
DAPF was programmed. Not yet tested on J716s hardware.]

---
 src/dapf.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dapf.c b/src/dapf.c
index 80dd53c8..15ec5145 100644
--- a/src/dapf.c
+++ b/src/dapf.c
@@ -199,8 +199,14 @@ struct entry {
 };
 
 struct entry dapf_entries[] = {
-    {"/arm-io/dart-aop", 1}, {"/arm-io/dart-mtp", 1},  {"/arm-io/dart-pmp", 1},
-    {"/arm-io/dart-isp", 5}, {"/arm-io/dart-isp0", 5}, {NULL, -1},
+    {"/arm-io/dart-aop", 1},
+    {"/arm-io/dart-mtp", 1},
+    {"/arm-io/dart-pmp", 1},
+    /* T6050: the PMP's DART is dart-pmp0 (dart,t8110; DAPF aperture reg[1], live-verified). */
+    {"/arm-io/dart-pmp0", 1},
+    {"/arm-io/dart-isp", 5},
+    {"/arm-io/dart-isp0", 5},
+    {NULL, -1},
 };
 
 int dapf_init_all(void)
